 {"type": "task", "attempts": 0, "created_by": "qa-cron", "id": "QA-TERMINAL-JAIL-13", "title": "[P1] unshare --kill-child teardown fails on a PIDNS-FULL clean host: orphaned sleep 300 survives wrapper SIGKILL for 15s (clean-machine only)", "status": "failed", "priority": "P1", "description": "QA lane tick terminal-jail-qa-2026-09-27-15-46-29 — fresh-system CI pass on bunker-las-02 (agent da4efd7a), synced tree at HEAD 6f61478. The native battery leg and the chaos-resource leg both failed on exactly one test: plugin/test_backend_parity.py::test_live_unshare_orphan_teardown — 'orphan: unshare payload 1906911 survived the wrapper's death for 15s'. Reproduced on the clean agent only: on the dev box at the same HEAD the full battery (plugin/ + tests/, 1444 passed / 7 skipped incl. integration markers) is green and this test passes in 0.44s. The test gates on _pidns_full() (host probe says namespaces work on the agent — no skip fired), spawns `terminal-jail --no-interruptor --user sleep 300` with TERMINAL_JAIL_JAIL_BACKEND=unshare, SIGKILLs the wrapper, and asserts the payload dies within 15s. On the clean agent the payload survived: --kill-child / PR_SET_PDEATHSIG teardown contract broken under the agent's namespace/user context. Other 8 parity tests incl. test_live_bwrap_orphan_teardown passed on the agent.", "detail": "Repro (clean agent): pytest plugin/test_backend_parity.py -x --tb=short -> 1 failed, 8 passed; FAILED plugin/test_backend_parity.py::test_live_unshare_orphan_teardown - Failed: orphan: unshare payload 1906911 survived the wrapper's death for 15s (assert at plugin/test_backend_parity.py:383). Control (dev box /home/kara/terminal-jail @ 6f61478): same test passes; full suite green. Cell statuses: ci-pass FAIL (native leg), chaos-resource FAIL (same single failure under 3G cap; cap verified child_saw=3145728). Every other test in both runs passed — the rc=1 is this one test, not a red suite.", "acceptance_criteria": "On a clean PIDNS-FULL host (no bubblewr